            "annotations": [],
            "logprobs": [],
            "text": "**Write the subject line as an imperative command that completes the sentence \"If applied, this commit will...\"**\n\nFor example:\n- ✅ `Fix race condition in session cleanup`\n- ❌ `Fixed some bugs` or `Changes to session stuff`\n\nThis keeps messages consistent with Git's own conventions (like \"Merge branch...\"), forces you to state *what* the commit does, and makes the history read like a clear list of actions when scanning `git log`.",
