            "text": "Under **Clause 2 (Termination)**, either party can terminate the agreement by giving **90 days' written notice**.\n\nThe contract doesn't say:\n- how the written notice has to be delivered (for example, by email, courier or registered mail)\n- whether the 90 days start when the notice is sent or when it's received\n- whether a party needs a reason, or \"cause,\" to terminate. Clause 2 doesn't require one, so it appears either party can end the agreement without giving a reason.\n\nClause 1 sets the agreement to run for 24 months from the Effective Date. The contract doesn't say how Clause 2 interacts with that term, such as whether a party can terminate early during those 24 months. The wording \"either party may terminate\" suggests it can, but the contract doesn't state this outright.",
