        "summary": [
          {
            "text": "Running the Euclidean algorithm on 1071 and 462: 1071 divided by 462 leaves remainder 147, 462 divided by 147 leaves 21, and 147 divides evenly by 21 — so the GCD is 21.\n\n",
            "type": "summary_text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "annotations": [],
            "logprobs": [],
            "text": "The greatest common divisor of 1071 and 462 is **21**.\n\nUsing the Euclidean algorithm:\n\n- 1071 = 2 × 462 + 147\n- 462 = 3 × 147 + 21\n- 147 = 7 × 21 + 0\n\nThe last nonzero remainder is 21.",
            "type": "output_text"
          }
        ],
        "id": "msg_kaeso_msg011CfvjfsNAiztELaa8xu1tC_1",
